    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33645" root="فرغ" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرَاغٌ</span></b>  [generally mentioned as an inf. n., and
much used as such; but accord. to the Msb, a
simple subst.: as a simple subst., it means <i>Emptiness, vacancy,</i> or <i>vacuity,</i> &amp;c.: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <i>vacancy,</i>
or <i>freedom,</i> from business, &amp;c.; or <i>contr. of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُغْلٌ</span>,
as is said in the K, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شغل</span>: and <i>cessation</i>
from an affair: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  &amp;c.: see 1]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيْتُ الفَرَاغِ</span>
means <i>The privy.</i>]

